<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gerrit Schotte</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1974</span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gerrit Schotte is a Curaçao politician who became the first prime minister of Curaçao when it became an autonomous country within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Kingdom of the Netherlands</a> on 10 October 2010. His government fell in 2012, and he was later convicted of corruption and money laundering.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gerrit-schotte.jpg" alt="Gerrit Schotte" width="320" height="225" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TeleCuracao Multimedia · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gerrit_Schotte_-_2.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
